# {{DIST}}

{{DESCRIPTION}}

{{SKILL_COUNT}} [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io) for [Flyte](https://flyte.org),
packaged for every agent harness — plus two MCP servers (`flyte-docs`, `flyte-cluster`)
for harnesses that read the bundled `.mcp.json`.

> `{{DIST}}` and `{{OTHER_DIST}}` are **identical mirrors** published from
> [the same repo]({{REPO_URL}}) at the same version. Install whichever name you
> prefer — installing both just gives you two copies of the same skills.

## Install

<!-- npm-only:start -->
### As a Claude Code plugin (npm source)

Add an entry to your marketplace's `marketplace.json`:

```json
{
  "name": "flyte",
  "source": { "source": "npm", "package": "{{DIST}}", "version": "^{{VERSION}}" }
}
```

Claude Code runs `npm install` and reads `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` from the
package root.

### As a CLI that copies skills into your harness

```bash
npx {{DIST}} install
```
<!-- npm-only:end -->
<!-- pypi-only:start -->
```bash
uvx {{DIST}} install
```

Or `pip install {{DIST}}` and then `{{DIST}} install`.
<!-- pypi-only:end -->

The CLI auto-detects which harnesses are set up on the machine and copies the
skills into each one's skills directory:

| Harness | User-level directory | Project-level (`--project`) |
|---|---|---|
| Claude Code | `~/.claude/skills/` | `.claude/skills/` |
| Codex CLI | `~/.agents/skills/` | `.agents/skills/` |
| opencode | `~/.config/opencode/skills/` | `.opencode/skills/` |
| pi | `~/.pi/agent/skills/` | — |

```bash
{{DIST}} install --target claude --target codex   # pick harnesses explicitly
{{DIST}} install --dir ./somewhere/skills         # arbitrary directory
{{DIST}} install --project                        # this repo only
{{DIST}} install --dry-run                        # show what would change
{{DIST}} uninstall                                # remove them again
{{DIST}} list                                     # list bundled skills
{{DIST}} path                                     # print the bundled plugin root
```

The MCP servers are **not** installed by the CLI — only the skills are. Harnesses
that consume the whole plugin (Claude Code, Codex) pick the servers up from
`.mcp.json` automatically.

## Native install paths

If you'd rather install from git than from a registry, the repo is a plugin
marketplace in its own right:

```
/plugin marketplace add flyteorg/flyte-agent-plugins
/plugin install flyte@flyte-agent-plugins
```

See [the repository README]({{REPO_URL}}#readme) for Codex, Hermes, opencode, and
pi instructions, the full skill list, and MCP server details.

